{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.5,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Decide and document whether a zizmor online-audit failure due to GitHub API outage/rate-limit/auth is gate-fatal, and add a fallback or explicit policy.","criteria":["error-handling","edge-cases","regression"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["_build-and-test.yml:99: `GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}` — online mode is now the CI default with no outage/rate-limit fallback","Ticket RCA comment: 'A deliberately invalid token scheduled all 40 but then failed the audit on a 401, proving online mode adds network/credential availability to the gate' and recommends 'decide explicitly whether API outage/rate-limit is gate-fatal'","ABSENCE: no timeout/continue-on-error/retry or documented failure policy is added around the online zizmor step"],"finding":"The online zizmor invocation adds a live GitHub-API dependency to the lint gate, but neither the Makefile, workflow, nor docs define behavior on API outage / rate-limit / auth failure. The RCA proved zizmor fails the audit (e.g. 401) when online and the token is invalid, and online mode makes network availability part of the gate — so a transient GitHub API outage or rate-limit will red the gating lint step with no fallback.","id":"0","impact":0.15,"location":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:90","norm_id":"n8c8727f24cc48104","priority":0.1313,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evid